Key Takeaways
auth.log ≠ wtmp. Authentication is not a session. One second of difference separates them — and that second is the whole point of Stage 3.

Correlate by PID. sshd[2491] in auth.log ↔ DEAD record in wtmp proves two artifacts describe the same event.

UTC everywhere. Set TZ=UTC, check the raw epoch, match the parser. Don't let a timezone shift ruin an answer.

Separate observation from inference. The log shows a download — not execution. Say what you saw, not what you assume.

A brute force has a fingerprint: one source, high speed, multiple usernames, throttling events. Learn to recognize it.

Distractors are real. 203.101.190.9 looks suspicious until you check the timeline and wtmp history. Evidence, not vibes.

